{
  "_about": "What a marked object of a layout does when poked (docs/art/scenes.md, Toys). A layout element with \"toy\": \"<type>\" becomes a toy of that type; \"toy_at\" gives the object's own box when the element is bigger than the object. kind: cutout = the object is taken out of the picture by an edit and lifted onto a card that moves; hotspot = nothing is taken away, the painting itself ripples, shakes or flashes. noun: how the edit's prompt names it. pivot: the point a cutout turns about (base = bottom centre, top = a hook it hangs from, centre). press: the answers to successive pokes, words of PaintedProp.VOCABULARY and sounds of assets/painted/sfx. A cutout that does not come off in the edit is a hotspot with the same answers. No line of text here: a text key would have to be in data/text/ru.json.",
  "types": {
    "lantern": {"kind": "cutout", "noun": "hanging lantern", "pivot": "top",
                "press": [{"do": "swing", "sound": "creak"}, {"do": "pulse", "sound": "chime"}, {"do": "rattle", "sound": "rattle"}]},
    "sundial": {"kind": "cutout", "noun": "sundial on its stone base", "pivot": "base",
                "press": [{"do": "wobble", "sound": "creak"}, {"do": "spin", "sound": "whoosh"}, {"do": "squash", "sound": "thunk"}]},
    "wheelbarrow": {"kind": "cutout", "noun": "wooden wheelbarrow", "pivot": "base",
